72 \u2014 strong toward **Pure Straight (16 points)**: 123, 456, 789 in same suit. I lack W1-W3 and W4-W6 groups.\n- But I have W1, W5, W6 \u2014 so if I keep W1, W5, W6, W7, W8, W9, I could form:\n  - [W5,W6,W7], [W7,W8,W9] (overlapping), [W8,W9,W?] no\n  - Or [W6,W7,W8], [W7,W8,W9] \u2014 possible with duplicate W7/W8.\n- But missing W2-W4 for lower chows.\n\nAlternatively, consider **Pure Shifted Chows** or **Short Straight** patterns \u2014 but current shape is fragmented.\n\nBest immediate goal: **Reduce useless tiles**. Among the valid plays:\n- Play W8: risky, as W8 is part of W789 chow.\n- Play W9: same risk.\n- Play W7, W6, W5: all mid-value, part of potential sequences.\n- Play F1, F2: both singleton winds, no pung.\n- Play J1: only dragon tile, might lose **All Types** if dropped.\n\nBut **All Types (6 points)** requires:\n- One tile from each of: Characters, Bamboos, Dots, Winds, Dragons.\nWe have:\n- Characters: yes (W1, etc.)\n- Bamboos: yes (meld [B6,B7,B8])\n- Dots: none in hand, none in melds \u2192 **currently NOT satisfying All Types**\nWait! Meld is [B6,B7,B8] \u2014 that\u2019s Bamboos (\u6761), not Dots (\u997c). We have no Dots tile anywhere.\n\nSo: **No tile of Dots (Bing) suit in hand or melds** \u2192 **All Types cannot be achieved unless we get a Dot tile**.\n\nThus, **dropping J1 won't break All Types** because **we already don't have Dots**.\n\nTherefore, **J1 is safe to discard** \u2014 we aren\u2019t completing All Types without a Dot tile anyway.\n\nSimilarly, F1 and F2 are singleton winds \u2014 no pung, hard to complete.\n\nNow, look at unshown tiles:\n- T9: 0 remaining \u2192 all discarded or used\n- B2: 1 left; B5: 2 left; B7: 1 left; B8: 2 left \u2014 consistent with game history\n\nBut more importantly: **Which discards are safer and improve hand structure?**\n\nI should aim for **Half Flush (16 points)**: four melds/pairs + one suit and honors.\n\nCurrent meld: [B6,B7,B8] (Bamboo) \u2014 this breaks Full Flush, but **Half Flush